To create the export component that allows users to select the type of document to export, you can implement a form with radio buttons or a dropdown menu for the format selection. Additionally, you should provide methods to handle each export option. Here's a basic example of how you might implement this in your Vue component:

```vue /shared/codx-junior/client/src/components/chat/ExportChat.vue
<template>
  <div>
    <h3>Export Chat</h3>
    <form @submit.prevent="exportChat">
      <label>
        <input type="radio" value="clipboard" v-model="exportFormat" />
        Copy to clipboard
      </label>
      <label>
        <input type="radio" value="markdown" v-model="exportFormat" />
        As document (markdown)
      </label>
      <label>
        <input type="radio" value="word" v-model="exportFormat" />
        As Word
      </label>
      <label>
        <input type="radio" value="pdf" v-model="exportFormat" />
        As PDF
      </label>
      <label>
        <input type="radio" value="excel" v-model="exportFormat" />
        As Excel
      </label>
      <button type="submit">Export</button>
    </form>
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  props: ['chat'],
  data() {
    return {
      exportFormat: 'clipboard', // Default export format
    };
  },
  methods: {
    exportChat() {
      switch (this.exportFormat) {
        case 'clipboard':
          this.copyToClipboard();
          break;
        case 'markdown':
          this.exportAsMarkdown();
          break;
        case 'word':
          this.exportAsWord();
          break;
        case 'pdf':
          this.exportAsPDF();
          break;
        case 'excel':
          this.exportAsExcel();
          break;
        default:
          console.error('Unsupported format');
      }
    },
    copyToClipboard() {
      // Logic to copy chat to clipboard
      console.log('Copying chat to clipboard...');
    },
    exportAsMarkdown() {
      // Logic to export chat as markdown
      console.log('Exporting chat as markdown...');
    },
    exportAsWord() {
      // Logic to export chat as Word
      console.log('Exporting chat as Word...');
    },
    exportAsPDF() {
      // Logic to export chat as PDF
      console.log('Exporting chat as PDF...');
    },
    exportAsExcel() {
      // Logic to export chat as Excel
      console.log('Exporting chat as Excel...');
    },
  },
};
</script>
```

In this implementation:
- The component has a form with radio buttons for each export format.
- The `exportFormat` data property holds the selected format.
- The `exportChat` method determines which format to export based on the selected option.
- Each export option has a corresponding method stub (e.g., `copyToClipboard`, `exportAsMarkdown`) where you can implement the specific logic for exporting the chat.
